/**
 * Bundled geography, pre-simplified. GENERATED — see scripts, do not hand-edit.
 *
 * ── Why the data is in the repo ──
 * A choropleth needs coastlines and there is no arithmetic that produces one.
 * Fetching them at render time would put a public CDN in the path of drawing a
 * slide, on networks that block exactly that; asking the model for coordinates
 * produces a country shaped like nothing. So it is downloaded once, simplified
 * to what a 900-point-wide slide can actually show, and shipped.
 *
 * Coordinates are [longitude, latitude] in degrees, one decimal place for the
 * world and finer for the two that matter most here. The projection happens at
 * render time, because the same outline has to work in a wide box and a tall one.
 *
 * Sources, all open data:
 *   world  — Natural Earth 1:110m via world-atlas (public domain)
 *   china  — geojson.cn province boundaries
 *   taiwan — ECharts map data, county level
 */

